{number: 130}
{title: Blessed Be The Fountain}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Blessed be the fountain of blood,
To a [Bb] world of [F] sinners re-[C7] vealed;
[F] Blessed be the dear Son of God:
Only [Bb] by His [C7] stripes we are [F] healed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
The [F] blood of Jesus cleanseth and washes as [Bb] white as the [F] snow;
Blessed be the [C7] fountain of blood,
Only [Bb] by His [C7] stripes we are [F] healed.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Though my sins were as scarlet,
He [Bb] washed them as [F] white as the [C7] snow;
[F] Blessed be the dear Son of God:
From His [Bb] side the [C7] healing streams [F] flow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Sing the praise of Jesus our King,
To the [Bb] ends of the [F] earth be it [C7] told;
[F] Blessed be the fountain of blood,
More [Bb] precious than [C7] silver and [F] gold.
{end_of_verse}
